Trackside
Trackside. A single line runs east to west past a signal box, whose door is at the top of a wooden stair. The points beside you are set for the main line.
You can see a tin box (which is closed) here.
> frame
Frame: 1N 2N 3N 4N. Mask 0. Train away, 0 through. Score 0.
> x points
The blades lie across for the main line.
> x signal
The home signal arm stands level, at danger.
> open tin box
You open the tin box, revealing a brass key.
A bell rings in the signal box.
> take key
Taken.
> listen
You hear nothing unexpected.
> unlock door with key
You unlock the box door.
A bell rings in the signal box.
> open door
You open the box door.
> u
Signal Box
Signal Box. A frame of four levers faces the window, with a block bell and a register on the shelf above.
You can see a red lever, a yellow lever, a blue lever, a black lever, a block bell and a train register here.
> listen
The block instrument ticks.
The block bell rings: three beats.
> x bell
A brass bell and a needle dial reading LINE BLOCKED.
> ring bell
Ring how many beats?
> ring 5
You ring 5 beats. Nobody answers.
The block bell rings: three beats.
> ring 12
That is not a bell code.
> pull 7
The levers are numbered 1 to 4.
> take lever 2
The levers only pull and push.
The block bell rings: three beats.
> x 4
Lever 4 works the points. It stands normal.
> ring 3
You ring three beats back. The needle swings to TRAIN ON LINE.
> x lever 3
Lever 3 works the facing point lock. It stands normal.
> x red lever
Lever 1 works the home signal. It stands normal.
A goods train draws up at the home signal and whistles.
> pull 2
Lever 2 is locked: lever 1 must be pulled first.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> pull 1
Lever 1 is locked: lever 3 must be pulled first.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> pull black lever
You heave the black lever over. The blades grind across.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> push 4
You push the black lever back. The blades grind across.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> push 4
Lever 4 is already normal.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> pull 3
You heave the blue lever over and the bolt shoots home.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> pull 4
Lever 4 is locked by lever 3.
The goods train whistles at the home signal.
> pull lever 1
You heave the red lever over and the wire clatters as the arm drops.
The goods train draws away past the box.
[The score has just gone up by one point.]
> pull 2
You heave the yellow lever over and the wire clatters as the arm drops.
> frame
Frame: 1R 2R 3R 4N. Mask 7. Train passed, 1 through. Score 1.
> ring 3
You ring three beats. Nobody answers.
> wait
Time passes.
> wait
Time passes.
> wait
Time passes.
> wait
Time passes.
> ring 2
Lever 1 is still over.
> push 1
Lever 1 is held over by lever 2.
> push 2
You push the yellow lever back and the arm rises to danger.
> push 1
You push the red lever back and the arm rises to danger.
> push 3
You push the blue lever back and the bolt withdraws.
> read register
The last lever moves are entered: 1 over, 2 over, 2 back, 1 back, 3 back.
> ring 2
You ring two beats: train out of section.
[The score has just gone up by one point.]
> frame
Frame: 1N 2N 3N 4N. Mask 0. Train away, 1 through. Score 2.
> pull 3
You heave the blue lever over and the bolt shoots home.
> pull 1
You heave the red lever over and the wire clatters as the arm drops.
The block bell rings: three beats.
> pull 2
You heave the yellow lever over and the wire clatters as the arm drops.
> x signal
The home signal arm stands off, lowered to clear. Below it the distant arm is off too.
> listen
The block instrument ticks.
The block bell rings: three beats.
> ring 3
You ring three beats back. The needle swings to TRAIN ON LINE.
> frame
Frame: 1R 2R 3R 4N. Mask 7. Train approaching, 2 to go, 1 through. Score 2.
> wait
Time passes.
> wait
Time passes.
The goods train runs through at speed, wagons rattling past the box.
[The score has just gone up by two points.]
